00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
have you ever wondered what career  opportunities a software engineer has  there are several career paths most  developers take  the first and obvious one is to grow in  the area in which you are working  if you are a junior developer then grow  to become a middle one then move into a  senior role and finally become a tech  lead  as a second option you can transition to  another technology stack  for example a significant number of  developers moved into the mobile area  when ios and android os gained ground  third you can grow into a managerial  role  there is a shortage of competent  managers out there  smart managers are expensive and they  are scarce  if the manager has a technical  background it will definitely allow him  to better understand his development  team and speak the same language  finally there is another option  you can become a software architect  and this will be the focus of today's  video  before moving forward it is necessary to  define the software architect role and  responsibilities  wikipedia defines this role as following  a software architect is a software  expert who makes high-level design  choices and dictates technical standards  including software coding standards  tools and platforms  like most high-level positions there are  no clear criteria that define this role  however it is possible to identify  several characteristics that contribute  to the career of the architect  the first characteristic of the software  architects is related to their ability  to master both deep and broad technical  knowledge  what this means is that they have  expertise in one or two technological  stacks at an expert level  which we can call deep knowledge  and at the same time have a decent  understanding of a few other ones  which we can call broad knowledge  when a person is good at many things  while specializing in a particular area  they can be viewed as a t-shaped person  a t-shaped person has deep knowledge in  one particular area and a broad base of  general supporting knowledge in multiple  other areas  if you represent this depth and breadth  visually you get a t shape  most software developers that are just  starting out usually find that their  knowledge or skill set looks more like  an eye a specialist with no broad  knowledge  for example a person might become a  javascript expert  some developers however move from one  project to another during the early  stages of their career development  acquiring a lot of diverse knowledge  without specializing in any particular  area  for example they can develop front-end  using html css and javascript on one  project and then move to mobile app  project and learn how to develop iphone  user interfaces  these developers would be considered a  dash shaped person  over time however the top software  developers learn how to combine  effectively both deep and broad  knowledge to become a t-shaped person  next characteristic of the software  architects is that they often assume  high level of responsibility in their  roles you should understand that  architect decisions are usually the most  expensive ones  therefore a person in this position  should take the most responsible  approach to his work and decisions made  if the developers error costs a couple  of days of work of one person  then the architect's mistake can cost  person years on complex projects  software architects have to make tough  decisions on a daily basis simply  because they are expected to do so  they are working with different people  from different areas  and have to deal with rapidly changing  demands or even with changing business  environments on a constant basis  therefore to be an effective software  architect  one has to learn how to make tough  decisions under stress  another important characteristic of the  software architects is the advanced  communication skills  communication is defined as the activity  of conveying information through the  exchange of thoughts and messages by  speech visuals signals writing or  behavior  you see technical background is  important to make technical decisions  but without proper communication it will  not be possible to get the information  necessary for the technical solution and  to sell it to the stakeholders  during the working day software  architects have to speak with customers  in the language of business stakeholders  and managers of all levels business  analysts as well as their development  team members  those who have a natural charisma and  know how to convince people have a huge  advantage in this role  in a nutshell effective software  architects are iconic eloquent and  competent speakers  to sum it up  here are the most important  characteristics of the software  architects  they have developed deep and broad  technical knowledge  they know how to take on responsibility  they are great communicators  it takes much more to be effective in  this role but these are considered the  most important traits that aspiring  software engineers should develop if  they want to become software architects  now let's discuss what software  architects do in their roles  here's the list of key job  responsibilities  identifying the key stakeholders on the  project  identifying business requirements and  requirements of the stakeholders  designing the entire system based on the  receive requirements  choosing the system architecture and  each component of this system  choosing the technologies for the  implementation of each component and  connections between the parts  code review  writing project documentation and  supporting it  creating unified development standards  in the company  this list of responsibilities is only a  subset of the software architect's job  duties the most important responsibility  is full technical support of the project  from the moment of inception  through product release to the  development of all of the consecutive  product features and enhancements  now imagine that you want to become a  software architect  where do you start  how do you achieve this objective  to begin with it is requisite to define  milestone goals that lead to achieving  your strategic objective of becoming a  software architect  these might include the following  milestone one  understand and try several technological  stacks  for example if your current knowledge is  concentrated in the field of ios it is  necessary to try android as well as  several server side languages such as  python or rust  alternatively if your current knowledge  is concentrated in the field of devops  you might want to consider learning  database engineering machine learning  and app security  milestone 2  reading literature  it is required to determine the most  valuable books and articles that will  help to grow in your direction of choice  usually the most effective way to find  such literature is to ask other  professionals in this field for their  recommendation  milestone three  obtain certificates  there are many certifications available  but only a few are worth their money  before starting however make sure that  the lecturer of the course is an  established professional in his field  and can answer your questions  milestone 4  find a mentor  it is desirable to find a software  architect at your current place of  employment  it is always easier to get experience  from a trained specialist than to start  considering a particular area from  scratch  be prepared to ask the right questions  from your mentor  as you move towards your strategic  objective of becoming a software  architect  one of the essential parts is a clear  and continuous plan review  you should always check what has been  done what should be reviewed and where  to accelerate or which goal to remove as  useless  however  even if you do not have a stable plan  available it is better to start taking  small steps that move you ahead rather  than remaining in the same place  know that this path might take several  years  the process of becoming a software  architect does not happen overnight  yet once you become a software architect  you will be able to create a lasting  impact on the organization you will be  employed by  and that's one of the best  accomplishments you might achieve in  life as a software engineer  if you found this video useful i'd  appreciate it if you smash the like  button and click on the notification  bell  also make sure to subscribe to the  coding tech channel for more videos like  this in the future

